    "body": "@atavistock here's the result on my end\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n~ ❯ time ~/.asdf/shims/elixir --short-version\r\n1.14.0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________\r\nExecuted in  242.90 millis    fish           external\r\n   usr time   52.35 millis    0.10 millis   52.25 millis\r\n   sys time  126.95 millis    2.04 millis  124.91 millis\r\n\r\n\r\n~ ❯ time ~/.asdf/installs/elixir/1.14.0-otp-25/bin/elixir --short-version\r\n1.14.0\r\n\r\n________________________________________________________\r\nExecuted in   31.20 millis    fish           external\r\n   usr time    2.96 millis    0.12 millis    2.84 millis\r\n   sys time   10.93 millis    3.25 millis    7.68 millis\r\n```\r\n\r\nasdf take a lot of time itself to locate the correct elixir.\r\nI haven't seen starship provide a way to to get the project folder(folder with .git), otherwise `cat .tool-versions` will save more time I think",
