    "created_at": "2025-01-05T05:20:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-01-05T05:21:58Z",
    "body": "If you use the [install scripts](https://elixir-lang.org/install.html#install-scripts) then this version seems to be pretty fast and it's possible to retrieve the OTP version as well:\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n[custom.elixir]\r\nformat = '[$symbol($output )]($style)'\r\ncommand = 'type elixir | sed -n \"s|.*/elixir/\\([0-9.]*\\)-otp-\\([0-9]*\\)/bin/elixir|v\\1 (OTP \\2)|p\"'\r\ndetect_files = ['mix.exs']\r\nstyle = 'bold purple'\r\nsymbol = '💧 '\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\n Here are the timings of modules in your prompt (>=1ms or output):\r\n custom.elixir  -   3ms  -   \"💧 v1.18.0 (OTP 27) \"\r\n character      -  <1ms  -   \"➜  \"\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
