    "updated_at": "2025-01-05T13:56:46Z",
    "body": "Nice find!\r\n\r\nThis looks like you are relying on the path containing the otp version using `type elixir`. It looks like this install script installs **both** Erlang and Elixir, which means it can put both versions in the path.\r\n\r\nI think most tools like `apt`, `pacman`, `brew`, etc and version managers ike `asdf`, `mise`, etc all expect Erlang as a separately installed package. So the path alone doesn't really have any information about the OTP version or potentially even the version of Elixir. Before the addition of `--short-version` the only reliable way to get the version was to run `elixir -v` which starts the whole VM just to print the version string.",
